  "_rising_tz_cases_comment": "Additive 2026-07-25 mutation-coverage fixtures for core/rising.js (Stryker survivor follow-up). Unlike rising_cases (fixed utcOffsetMinutes, legacy getRisingSign API), these carry an IANA tz string and are consumed via computeRising/offsetMinutesForWallTime so they exercise the two-pass DST-resolution path (core/rising.js L135-144), not just ascendantDeg. expected.risingSign values are sourced from an independent Swiss Ephemeris computation (pyswisseph, the same ephemeris engine astro.com's charts are built on; astro.com itself was unreachable from the build environment) cross-validated to <0.01deg against the three existing astro.com-anchored reference cases before use, then to <1deg agreement across 2000 random valid inputs against an independently-written from-formula implementation. expected.offsetMinutes values are sourced separately, by tracing the documented two-pass algorithm against directly-probed real Intl.DateTimeFormat output (not by executing core/rising.js).",
  "rising_tz_cases": [
    {
      "label": "America/New_York spring-forward 2023-03-12 02:30 (skipped hour) resolves via the o2 (EDT) pass, not the o1 (EST) guess",
      "dob": "2023-03-12",
      "time": "02:30",
      "tz": "America/New_York",
      "lat": 40.7128,
      "lng": -74.006,
      "expected": {
        "risingSign": "sagittarius",
        "offsetMinutes": -240
      }
    },
    {
      "label": "Asia/Kolkata pre-1906 MMT (1905-12-31 21:00): o2 falls on the seconds-precision Madras Mean Time string (GMT+05:21:10) and fails to parse, offset falls back to o1 (IST)",
